{"timestamp": "2026-08-06T05:26:38.676978+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-52417d9b-4b7f-4d5a-8ca6-5f44baef9736', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You choose the physical form of every block in one lesson.\\n\\nThe teaching is already decided and is not yours to change. Each block has a\\njob and a brief. You choose the shape on the page that carries it with the\\nleast machinery, and you choose for the whole lesson at once so the document\\nhas rhythm rather than a run of identical shapes.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING\\n\\n  Resource: Lesson (lesson)\\n\\n  A lesson is the default full teaching resource. It introduces a concept,\\n  builds understanding, models the method, gives students guided-to-independent\\n  practice, and closes with a retention check.\\n  \\n  A lesson teaches before it asks students to perform independently. It is not\\n  a worksheet, not a quick reference, and not a quiz. The teacher should be\\n  able to use it as the main classroom arc for first contact with a concept.\\n  \\n  The pedagogical arc is: orient -> build -> model -> practice -> close.\\n  Every section must serve that arc. The planner must not skip the modelling\\n  step, and it must not turn the close into a second teaching section.\\n\\n  Use when:\\n    - First exposure to a new concept\\n    - A full classroom lesson with explicit teaching and practice\\n    - When the teacher wants one coherent teaching arc from hook to check\\n    - When learners need explanation before independent work\\n  Never when:\\n    - The teacher only wants practice questions - use a worksheet or practice set\\n    - The teacher only wants a fast definition or reminder - use a quick explainer\\n    - The session is primarily assessment - use a quiz or exit ticket\\n    - Students already know the concept and only need repetition\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE GIVEN\\n\\n  arc               how this lesson moves, from the teaching plan\\n  sections          in order, each with its blocks\\n  per block         id, position, intent, brief\\n  available_objects per intent \u2014 the forms that intent permits, narrowed to\\n                    the forms this resource allows. Each carries:\\n                      holds\\n                      earns_its_place_when\\n                      reject_when\\n                      capacity\\n                      placement\\n\\navailable_objects is closed. An object not shown for an intent is not\\navailable for that block, whatever you may know about it.\\n\\n## THE DEFAULT IS PROSE\\n\\nProse is the cheapest form. It carries almost anything. Every other object\\nmust earn its place against it.\\n\\nRead `earns_its_place_when`. If the brief does not already satisfy it, the\\nobject is out \u2014 even when it appears in available_objects. Then read\\n`reject_when` as the counter-test.\\n\\nThe question is never \"could this be a table?\" It is \"does this brief already\\ncontain what a table needs?\"\\n\\n## WORKED DECISION\\n\\n  block: explain-b1\\n  intent: compare\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants by listing what was held the same \u2014 same\\n          pot, same soil, same water \u2014 and identify light as the only\\n          condition that differed.\"\\n  available_objects: [table, prose, questions]\\n\\n    table\\n      earns_its_place_when: two or more columns of comparable values AND two\\n                            or more rows, with every cell fillable\\n      -> two plants x four conditions. Every cell fillable. Earned.\\n\\n    prose\\n      -> would make the reader hold eight facts in sequence and build the\\n         comparison themselves.\\n\\n    questions\\n      -> the brief says compare, not ask.\\n\\n  -> table\\n\\n  Same intent, different brief:\\n\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants only on whether they received light.\"\\n\\n    table -> one condition, two rows. reject_when: one column of values.\\n  -> prose\\n\\nThe intent did not change. The brief decided the form.\\n\\n## CAPACITY IS REAL\\n\\n`capacity` states what the printed page holds. It is not a style preference.\\n\\nIf the brief needs more than the object\\'s capacity, the object is wrong.\\n\\n  aside          bodyMaxWords 40. The margin column is 56mm. A point needing\\n                 80 words does not become a small aside; it is prose.\\n  aside          maxPerSection 2. A third aside in one section collides with\\n                 the two already floated.\\n  table          columnsMax 4. A fifth column does not fit the main column\\n                 with a readable header.\\n  list           itemsMin 3. Two bullets is a sentence.\\n  choices        optionsMin 3.\\n\\nNever choose an object expecting the writer to compress. The writer will\\neither overflow or cut something that mattered.\\n\\n## RHYTHM ACROSS THE LESSON\\n\\nYou see the whole lesson. Use that.\\n\\nA section-by-section chooser cannot see this:\\n\\n    ORIENT     figure\\n    EXPLAIN    figure\\n    CONFRONT   figure\\n    CHECK      questions\\n\\nEvery choice locally defensible; the document visually flat. You can see it,\\nso prevent it.\\n\\nGuidance, not arithmetic:\\n\\n  - Avoid the same object three times in a row unless the briefs genuinely\\n    demand it. If they do, say so in `reason`.\\n  - Avoid every section opening with the same form.\\n  - Figures are expensive and slow. Two per lesson is usually plenty, and\\n    they should sit where something is genuinely hard to say in words.\\n  - Do not manufacture variety. Two prose blocks in a row are sometimes\\n    exactly right. A table with nothing to tabulate is worse than a run of\\n    prose.\\n\\nVariety serves reading. It is not a quota.\\n\\n## PLACEMENT\\n\\nOnly `aside` may take the margin. Everything else sits in the main column.\\n\\nChoose margin when the point is genuinely parenthetical: true, useful, and not\\npart of the argument the reader is following. Choose main when the reader\\nneeds it in sequence.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU MAY NOT CHANGE\\n\\n  block id\\n  position\\n  section order\\n  intent\\n  brief\\n  evidence_refs, evidence, departure_reason\\n  source_question_ids\\n\\nYou add a form. You change nothing else. If a brief looks wrong to you, choose\\nthe best form for it anyway and note the concern in `reason`.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n  Never choose outside available_objects for that block.\\n  Never choose an object whose earns_its_place_when the brief does not meet.\\n  Never choose an object whose capacity the brief exceeds.\\n  Never choose `heading`. Headings come from section titles.\\n  Never choose `answer-key`. It is produced at document level.\\n  Never add a figure because a section looks plain.\\n  Never give one block two objects, or leave a block without one.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only. No preamble, no code fences.\\n\\n{\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"slot_id\": str,\\n      \"forms\": [\\n        {\\n          \"block_id\": str,\\n          \"object\": str,\\n          \"placement\": \"main\" | \"margin\",\\n          \"reason\": str,\\n          \"escalation\": str | null\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n`reason` \u2014 which `earns_its_place_when` clause this brief satisfies, and how.\\nBe specific to this brief. A reason that would fit any brief is not a reason.\\n\\n`escalation` \u2014 if you did not choose prose, what prose would have lost. Null\\nwhen you chose prose.\\n\\nEvery block in the teaching plan must appear exactly once. No extras.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n  1. Would prose have worked? If yes, why did I not use it?\\n  2. Does the brief actually contain what this object needs, or am I assuming\\n     the writer will produce it?\\n  3. Does the brief fit inside capacity? Count, do not estimate.\\n  4. Read my form choices top to bottom. Does the lesson have rhythm, or is\\n     it three of one thing?\\n  5. Did I add variety that no brief asked for?\\n  6. Does every block from the teaching plan appear exactly once?\\n  7. Is any `reason` generic enough to fit a different block?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FormPlanBlock\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"position\": {\"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"intent\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"brief\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_refs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"departure_reason\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source_question_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"object\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"placement\": {\"default\": \"main\", \"enum\": [\"main\", \"margin\", \"spanning\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"position\", \"intent\", \"brief\", \"object\"], \"title\": \"FormPlanBlock\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FormPlanSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"slot_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"blocks\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormPlanBlock\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"slot_id\"], \"title\": \"FormPlanSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormPlanSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"title\": \"FormPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"arc\": \"The lesson opens on two basil plants\\\\u2014one lush on a sunny windowsill, one stunted in a dark corner\\\\u2014to spark the question why the dark plant can\\\\u2019t make food despite having water and air. It builds the model that light provides the energy to combine water and air inside leaves into food, and that without this energy the plant cannot produce food to grow. It confronts the mistake that sunlight is the plant\\\\u2019s food, showing that light\\\\u2019s role is as energy, not a meal, and closes by checking whether learners can explain why a plant fails in darkness.\",\\n  \"available_objects\": {\\n    \"by_intent\": {\\n      \"activate-prior-knowledge\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"answer-key\": [],\\n      \"apply\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"check-understanding\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"classify\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"compare\": [\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-back\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-forward\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"define\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"demonstrate\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"derive\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"diagnose-misconception\": [\\n        \"choices\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"emphasise\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"evaluate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain-cause\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"interpret\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"investigate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"memory-aid\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"model-thinking\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"name-parts\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"orient\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-guided\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-independent\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"reflect\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"sequence\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"show-structure\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"state-goal\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"summarise\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"trace-flow\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"transfer\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"warn\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"objects\": [\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"bodyMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"labelMaxWords\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"maxPerSection\\\\\": 2}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"memory-aid\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"One short point that must sit outside the reading line without breaking it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"aside\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Longer than the margin column holds, or the point belongs in the flow. If it will not fit in 40 words it is prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'margin\\', \\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"optionMaxWords\\\\\": 15, \\\\\"optionsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"optionsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Selection is the response AND every wrong option carries diagnostic meaning.\",\\n        \"id\": \"choices\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Distractors are filler, or the answer cannot be reduced to a selectable option.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"altTextMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 30}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Spatial, sequential, or structural content the reader would otherwise have to construct mentally.\",\\n        \"id\": \"figure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Decorative, or the caption would restate the surrounding prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"leadInMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"wordsPerItem\\\\\": 25}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Three or more genuinely parallel items that lose nothing when the connective prose between them is removed.\",\\n        \"id\": \"list\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fewer than three items, or items that need explaining to one another. Two bullets is a sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'margin\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"paragraphsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"paragraphsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"wordsPerParagraph\\\\\": 120}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Default. Use unless another object earns its place against it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"prose\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Never rejected. Prose is the fallback.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 6, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 45}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"The learner must produce something in their own words or working.\",\\n        \"id\": \"questions\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fixed options exist \\\\u2014 use choices. Or nothing is actually being asked.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"columnsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"columnsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"rowsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"rowsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"wordsPerCell\\\\\": 12}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Two or more columns of comparable values AND two or more rows, with every cell fillable.\",\\n        \"id\": \"table\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"One column of values, or any cell that would be empty, \\'n/a\\', or a full sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"problemMaxWords\\\\\": 60, \\\\\"stepsMax\\\\\": 7, \\\\\"stepsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"wordsPerStep\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"A complete instance from setup to answer, with every step visible.\",\\n        \"id\": \"worked-example\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"No final answer, or steps the learner is meant to supply themselves.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"05fddc80790c232176df5c03bf7ea1ead8b910d06c848b4836be205a7552c98b\"\\n  },\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Show the two basil plants: windowsill plant lush and green, dark corner plant small and yellow. Ask: \\\\u2018The dark plant has water and air, but it is not growing. What is it missing that prevents it from making food?\\\\u2019 Keep the question open.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The anchor provides a concrete phenomenon; the orient intent begins with an observation and raises a reason to learn.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"anchor-1\",\\n            \"lesson.objective\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n          \"position\": 0,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Prompt recall: \\\\u2018We know plants are producers that make their own food. What three things do they need? (light, water, air).\\\\u2019 Briefly confirm: plants use light, water, and air to make food in their leaves. Do not introduce new terms.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The objective requires recognising light, water, and air as inputs; these prior knowledge items cover that understanding.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"prior-3\",\\n            \"prior-4\",\\n            \"prior-5\",\\n            \"lesson.objective\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"position\": 1,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"specific_purpose\": \"Hook attention with the contrasting plants and surface what learners already know about plants making food.\",\\n      \"transition\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Identify the key players: leaves (where food is made), water (absorbed by roots, travels up stem), air (enters leaves from surroundings), light energy (from sunlight), and food (the result plants need to grow). Use the windowsill basil as an example: \\\\u2018Its leaves get air, its roots soak up water, and sunlight shines on its leaves.\\\\u2019\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The lesson must name the components before explaining the mechanism; prior knowledge covers the site of food production, water absorption, and the inputs of light, water, air.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"prior-4\",\\n            \"prior-5\",\\n            \"prior-6\",\\n            \"prior-7\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"name-parts\",\\n          \"position\": 0,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"State the causal link: \\\\u2018Light energy is the essential driver. It provides the power to join water and air together in the leaves to build food. It is not a raw material \\\\u2014 it is the energy that makes the reaction happen.\\\\u2019 Use an analogy: like the energy from a whisk beats eggs and flour into cake batter; without the whisk\\\\u2019s motion, the ingredients stay separate.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The objective requires explaining why light is necessary, which demands a causal account linking energy to the combination of ingredients.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"lesson.objective\",\\n            \"must-2\",\\n            \"must-3\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"position\": 1,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Return to the anchor: point to the dark corner plant. \\\\u2018It has water, it has air, but it gets almost no light. Without light energy, the leaves cannot combine those ingredients into food. The plant cannot make food, so it cannot grow.\\\\u2019 Contrast with the windowsill plant that gets light energy and makes food, growing lush.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The anchor offers two concrete cases differing only in light; a comparison makes the causal role of light vivid and grounds the \\\\u2018must\\\\u2011establish\\\\u2019 point that without light, no food is made.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"anchor-1\",\\n            \"must-5\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"explain-b3\",\\n          \"intent\": \"compare\",\\n          \"position\": 2,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"specific_purpose\": \"Build the causal model that light energy drives the combination of water and air in leaves, and show why its absence stops food production.\",\\n      \"transition\": \"Now that learners are curious about what the dark plant lacks, we build the full model of how light energy, water, and air work together.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Present the belief: \\\\u2018Some people think sunlight is the plant\\\\u2019s food \\\\u2014 that plants eat light, and water and air are just extras. It seems right because plants grow toward light, and without light they look starved.\\\\u2019 Ask: \\\\u2018If sunlight is food, then a plant in the dark should be hungry and could grow if we just gave it more sunlight directly. But is that the whole story?\\\\u2019\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"M1 states sunlight as food; naming this belief and why it feels plausible is necessary before showing it fails.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"M1\",\\n            \"lesson.objective\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"confront-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"position\": 0,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Reveal the failure: \\\\u2018If light were food, the dark corner plant could be \\\\\"fed\\\\\" light and would grow, even without water and air? No \\\\u2014 if we give it water and air but no light, it still fails. Light is energy to combine ingredients, not the meal. The dark plant has ingredients but no energy to cook them; the sunny plant has both ingredients and energy.\\\\u2019 Ground this in the anchor: the dark basil has water and air but no light energy, so it cannot make food.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The dark anchor plant disproves the \\\\u2018light as food\\\\u2019 error because it has water and air but still fails; the correct model \\\\u2014 light as energy \\\\u2014 explains the failure.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"anchor-1\",\\n            \"must-2\",\\n            \"must-5\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"confront-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"explain\",\\n          \"position\": 1,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": []\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"confront\",\\n      \"specific_purpose\": \"Surface the misconception that sunlight is the plant\\\\u2019s food and show it failing against the anchor, reinforcing the energy model.\",\\n      \"transition\": \"With the model in place, we address a common mistake about what light really provides.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Administer the items that test understanding of why the dark basil plant cannot produce food, expecting the answer that light energy is essential to combine water and air in leaves.\",\\n          \"departure_reason\": null,\\n          \"evidence\": \"The items directly probe the objective and the must\\\\u2011establish point that without light, plants cannot make food; the anchor scenario provides the concrete case.\",\\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\\n            \"lesson.objective\",\\n            \"must-5\",\\n            \"anchor-1\"\\n          ],\\n          \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"position\": 0,\\n          \"source_question_ids\": [\\n            \"890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:93aa315e-fa1d-4798-be6e-0ceb17544a40.i1\",\\n            \"890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:93aa315e-fa1d-4798-be6e-0ceb17544a40.i2\",\\n            \"890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:93aa315e-fa1d-4798-be6e-0ceb17544a40.i3\",\\n            \"890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:93aa315e-fa1d-4798-be6e-0ceb17544a40.i4\",\\n            \"890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:890c7cb8-5ccb-4b31-adbb-fb336b766e14:93aa315e-fa1d-4798-be6e-0ceb17544a40.i5\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"specific_purpose\": \"Diagnose whether learners can apply the correct idea to explain why a plant in the dark cannot make food.\",\\n      \"transition\": \"Now we check whether learners can explain why a plant fails in the dark, using the correct role of light energy.\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'reasoning_effort': 'low', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
